    "short_description": "The Wall Street Journal (WSJ) is a prominent American daily business and financial newspaper based in Midtown Manhattan, New York City. Founded on July 8, 1889, by Charles Dow, Edward Jones, and Charles Bergstresser, it is published six days a week by Dow Jones & Company, a division of News Corp. The WSJ operates on a subscription model, providing access to a wide range of content, including business, finance, politics, arts, culture, and lifestyle.\n\nThe WSJ offers various products and services, including a daily print edition, digital subscriptions, mobile apps for real-time news, and international editions tailored for different regions. It also publishes WSJ Magazine, which focuses on lifestyle and design. With a reputation for unbiased reporting and a generally conservative editorial stance, the WSJ is recognized as a leading source for financial news, boasting over 4 million digital subscribers and winning 37 Pulitzer Prizes for outstanding journalism. Its target audience includes global professionals, investors, and business leaders seeking authoritative coverage of commerce and finance.",
